Subject: [PATCH 12/13] [M156] FSA: block remote desktop client-drive UNC paths
 on Windows

Original change's description:
> FSA: block remote desktop client-drive UNC paths on Windows
>
> Inside Windows Remote Desktop Services (RDP, Azure Virtual Desktop,
> Windows 365, Hyper-V Enhanced Session, and Horizon TSDR) and Citrix HDX
> Client Drive Mapping sessions, the client machine's drives and shared
> folders are exposed via the \\tsclient and \\Client UNC redirectors.
> Because "tsclient" and "Client" are valid DNS names and drive-letter
> blocklist rules only match the session host's local drives, non-admin
> redirected paths such as \\tsclient\C\Users\<user>\.ssh or
> \\Client\C\Users\<user>\.bashrc were not caught by MaybeIsLocalUNCPath()
> or ShouldBlockAccessToPath().
>
> Add "tsclient" and "client" to IsLocalUNCServer() so sensitive-entry
> checks reject remote-session client-drive UNC paths (including case
> variants, forward-slash UNC syntax, and trailing-dot FQDN forms).
>
